Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:25:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bearer-qmi: don't enable the WDS event report indications

event_report_indication_cb() only logs that a report arrived, so none of the
twelve indications requested on connect is used. On the Nothing Phone (1)
(SM7325) the modem sends these event reports while the system is suspended
and each one wakes it: the first QRTR packet after 5 of 8 automatic wakes in
an hour was a WDS Event Report indication (0x0001) to ModemManager's client,
in bursts of 2-3 wakes a few seconds apart.

Request the indications disabled on connect, as the cleanup path already
does. Connection status changes keep arriving through the Packet Service
Status indications.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mm-bearer-qmi.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mm-bearer-qmi.c b/src/mm-bearer-qmi.c
index 64d983eb..62fe528d 100644
--- a/src/mm-bearer-qmi.c
+++ b/src/mm-bearer-qmi.c
@@ -1533,7 +1533,13 @@ setup_event_report_unsolicited_events (MMBearerQmi *self,
                                        GAsyncReadyCallback callback,
                                        gpointer user_data)
 {
-    QmiMessageWdsSetEventReportInput *input = event_report_input_new (TRUE);
+    /* The event report indication handler only logs that the report was
+     * received, so none of these indications is used. Enabling them made
+     * the modem send an event report (dormancy, bearer technology, channel
+     * rate...) that woke a suspended system every few minutes; request them
+     * disabled instead. Connection status changes still come through the
+     * "Packet Service Status" indications. */
+    QmiMessageWdsSetEventReportInput *input = event_report_input_new (FALSE);
 
     qmi_client_wds_set_event_report (client,
                                      input,
